      V.about = () =>
        `<section><div class="wrap cols"><div class="rv sticky-photo"><img src="${PORTRAIT}" alt="Portrait of Tiyasha Babu" loading="lazy" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:4/5;object-fit:cover;object-position:center 30%;display:block"></div><div class="rv"><span class="lab">About</span><h1 class="h2">ABOUT ME</h1><p class="serif" style="font-size:clamp(24px,3vw,34px);line-height:1.2">Someone who notices how stories get built — and wants to build them for brands.</p><p>I’m a final-year B.Sc. Media Science student specialising in Integrated Marketing Communication, interested in the space where creativity, communication and strategy meet.</p><p>I started with the making — cameras, edits, scripts, shoots and stories. But somewhere along the way, I became more interested in the question behind the content:</p><p class="serif" style="font-size:24px;color:var(--ac);line-height:1.3">Why should this exist? Who is it for? And what should it make someone feel, think or do?</p><p>That question pulled me towards marketing.</p><p>Today, I’m exploring social media, brand communication, content strategy and creative marketing — while bringing with me a hands-on understanding of how content is actually made.</p><span class="lab" style="margin-top:40px">Who I am</span><p>Final-year B.Sc. Media Science<br>Specialisation: Integrated Marketing Communication<br>Based in: Kolkata, India</p><span class="lab" style="margin-top:40px">My journey</span><p class="serif" style="font-size:22px;line-height:1.5">Media Science → Making Content → Integrated Marketing Communication → Media Experience → Social Media → Brand Communication → Marketing</p><p>I’ve moved from being primarily interested in how to make something to becoming equally curious about why it should be made in the first place.</p><span class="lab" style="margin-top:40px">What I’ve done</span><a href="#/work/radio-mirchi" class="rv" style="display:block;border-top:1px solid var(--ln);padding:16px 0"><h3 style="font-size:28px">Radio Mirchi Kolkata</h3><span class="mu" style="font-size:14px">Social media · Content · Reels · Campaign production · AI-assisted content · Creative production</span></a><a href="#/work/yuva-tourism-club" class="rv" style="display:block;border-top:1px solid var(--ln);padding:16px 0"><h3 style="font-size:28px">Yuva Tourism Club</h3><span class="mu" style="font-size:14px">Social media management · Content planning · Caption writing · Event communication · Creative design</span></a><a href="#/work/itrea" class="rv" style="display:block;border-top:1px solid var(--ln);padding:16px 0"><h3 style="font-size:28px">Itréa Fragrances</h3><span class="mu" style="font-size:14px">Brand storytelling · Website content · Product communication · Editorial content · Creative direction</span></a><a href="#/work/aynapuri" class="rv" style="display:block;border-top:1px solid var(--ln);padding:16px 0"><h3 style="font-size:28px">Creative Media Projects</h3><span class="mu" style="font-size:14px">Cinematography · Direction · Editing · Documentary · Visual storytelling</span></a><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--ln)"></div><span class="lab" style="margin-top:40px">What I’m looking for</span><p>I’m looking for opportunities where I can learn, contribute and get closer to the kind of work I want to build a career in:</p>${words(["Marketing", "Social Media & Digital Marketing", "Brand Communication", "Content Strategy", "Advertising & Creative Strategy"])}<p style="margin-top:14px">I’m especially drawn to work where there’s room to think, create, experiment and collaborate — rather than simply execute the same thing every day.</p><span class="lab" style="margin-top:40px">Beyond work</span><p>Outside work, I’m usually watching films, collecting ideas, noticing good branding, taking too many photos, discovering new places, or overthinking why a particular advertisement made me stop scrolling.</p><p>I’m drawn to stories, music, cities, visual details and the little things that make ordinary moments memorable.</p><p class="serif" style="font-size:22px">I think most good ideas start with simply paying attention.</p><span class="lab" style="margin-top:40px">Currently</span><p class="tiny">Learning. Making. Experimenting. Figuring out what makes people stop, look, feel and remember.</p><a class="btn" href="#/skills">WHAT I WORK WITH →</a></div></div></section>`;
